1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Wang Guizhi 王珪之 (fl. 474–480), Liu-Song period historian.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wang Guizhi’s ancestral home was Linyi 臨沂 in Langye 琅邪 commandery (modern Linyi, Shandong). He was a younger cousin of Wang Qunzhi 王逡之 (d. 495). In 474, the imperial court commissioned him to compile a history of bureaucratic offi
2 CONC ces, appointment procedures, and official apparel. At the beginning of the Southern Qi, Chu Yuan 褚淵 (435–482) was assigned to revise the work. Wang Guizhi died before he could complete editing the final version. In 491, Wang Guizh
2 CONC i’s son Wang Hao 王顥 presented the completed fifty-''juan'' work to the court. It was titled ''Qi zhi yi'' 齊職儀 (Official protocol of the Qi).
2 CONT
2 CONT David R. Knechtges
2 CONT
2 CONT Citation
2 CONT * 王珪之 Wang Guizhi, Brill’s Chinese Reference Shelf. Brill Online, 2017. http://chinesereferenceshelf.brillonline.com/ancient-literature/entries/COM-0158
