1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.chinaknowledge.de/History/Zhou/zhou-rulers.html
2 CONT
2 CONT The ancestress of the Zhou, Jiangyuan 姜嫄 (daughter of a noble called Youtai 有邰 and wife of Emperor Di Ku (Diku) 帝嚳), is said to have conceived after stepping into the footsteps of the Shang Dynasty god Shangdi 上帝, giving birth to 
2 CONC the Lord of Millet (Hou Ji, Houji 后稷). The Zhou rulers are therefore thought to be descendants of the Yellow Emperor (Huangdi 黃帝). Before settling down in the Wei River 渭水 valley/Shaanxi, the Zhou people is said to have lived near
2 CONC  Bin 豳 (or 邠) in the Fen River 汾水 valley (modern Shanxi; other interpretations locate Bin in the Jing River 涇水 valley north of modern Xi'an 西安/Shaanxi). 
