1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://cbdb.fas.harvard.edu/cbdbapi/person.php?id=8162 '''Wu Kui''' 吳奎] [8162] His ancestors lived in Jinan, Yucheng xian. During the disorder of the Five Dynasties, at some unknown generation, the family moved t
2 CONC o Weizhou, Beihai xian. None of his patrilineal ancestors of the previous three generations held office. His mother's father Wang(2) Ting(2) [3981], a Weizhou, Beihai resident, attempted to pass the mingjing exam and failed. He la
2 CONC ter became the prefectural teacher (zhujiao). The father of his first wife, Zhao(1) Li [3204], was a county magistrate, from a wealthy Jizhou, Xindu xian family. When Kui was twenty, he had already gained a reputation as a classic
2 CONC al scholar and Zhao(1) Li made him his son-in-law despite the fact that the Wu(3) family was considered to be quite poor. Zhao(1) Shi was Jing's [1963] mother. His second wife's father, Zhang(1) Yu(2) [3176], had a nominal title. 
